        "role": "user",
        "content": "{\"context\":[{\"id\":\"c1\",\"text\":\"We continue to focus on managing inventory and other working capital requirements.\"},{\"id\":\"c2\",\"text\":\"Days sales outstanding relating to trade accounts receivable was 53 days at March 31, 2026, 51 days at June 30, 2025 and 53 days at March 31, 2025.\"},{\"id\":\"c3\",\"text\":\"Days supply of inventory on hand was 88 days at March 31, 2026, 82 days at June 30, 2025 and 85 days at March 31, 2025.\"},{\"id\":\"c4\",\"text\":\"Net cash (used in) provided by investing activities decreased by $1.6 billion in the first nine months of fiscal 2026 compared to the first nine months of fiscal 2025.\"}],\"filing\":\"PH 10-Q\",\"section\":\"Part I Item 2\",\"sentences\":[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Cash Flows\",\"text\":\"The decrease was primarily attributable to $1.0 billion in cash used for the Curtis acquisition and lower proceeds from sale of businesses in fiscal 2026.\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Cash Flows\",\"text\":\"Proceeds from sale of businesses in fiscal 2025 included net proceeds of $621 million related to the divestitures of the composites and fuel containment business and the non-core filtration business.\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Cash Flows\",\"text\":\"Net cash used in financing activities for the first nine months of fiscal 2026 and 2025 were impacted by the following factors:\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Cash Flows\",\"text\":\"Net commercial paper borrowings of $323 million in the first nine months of fiscal 2026 compared to net commercial paper repayments of $213 million in the first nine months of fiscal 2025.\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Cash Flows\",\"text\":\"During the first nine months of fiscal 2025, we made principal payments of $490 million on our term loan facility and $500 million in connection with the maturity of medium-term notes.\"},{\"id\":\"s6\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Cash Flows\",\"text\":\"Additionally, we issued €700 million aggregate principal amount of 2.90 percent Senior Notes due 2030, the proceeds of which were used to repay the €700 million aggregate principal amount of 1.125 percent Senior Notes due 2025.\"},{\"id\":\"s7\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Cash Flows\",\"text\":\"There were no comparable transactions during the first nine months of fiscal 2026.\"},{\"id\":\"s8\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Cash Flows\",\"text\":\"Repurchases under our share repurchase program amounted to 1.0 million common shares for $825 million during the first nine months of fiscal 2026, compared to 1.2 million common shares for $750 million during the first nine months of fiscal 2025.\"},{\"id\":\"s9\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Debt\",\"text\":\"To fund short-term liquidity needs, we utilize a commercial paper program that is supported by our revolving credit agreement.\"},{\"id\":\"s10\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Debt\",\"text\":\"In August 2025, we amended our revolving credit agreement to increase the total line of credit to $3.75 billion, and authorized a corresponding increase in the commercial paper program size to $3.75 billion.\"},{\"id\":\"s11\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Debt\",\"text\":\"The revolving credit agreement expires in June 2028; however, we have the right to request a one-year extension of the expiration date.\"},{\"id\":\"s12\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Debt\",\"text\":\"Advances from the credit agreement can be used for general corporate purposes, including acquisitions, and for the refinancing of existing indebtedness.\"},{\"id\":\"s13\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Debt\",\"text\":\"Issuances of commercial paper reduce the amount of credit available under the revolving credit agreement.\"},{\"id\":\"s14\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Debt\",\"text\":\"As of March 31, 2026, there were no borrowings outstanding under the revolving credit agreement, and commercial paper notes outstanding were $2.1 billion.\"},{\"id\":\"s15\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Debt\",\"text\":\"Taking into account outstanding commercial paper notes, $1.7 billion was available for borrowing under the credit agreement as of March 31, 2026.\"}]}"
      }
